From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:35:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Hand the PMP to Linux

The internal display coprocessor takes its DISP power vote through the
PMP (pmp-display.c: the "pmp" alias names the owner, and the loader
supplies apple,tunable-soc-device). The J604 device tree does not ask
the loader for the PMP, so with the display handed over the DCP would
find no supplier and keep the boot framebuffer.

Ask for it the way the J713 does (aurora-silicon/linux t8132-j713.dts):

- the "pmp" alias, so that m1n1 copies this Mac's PMP values from the
  Apple device tree onto the node and enables it;
- /arm-io/pmp in linux-enablement-mac,dapf-handoff and
  linux-enablement-mac,dapf-power-on-handoff, so that m1n1 powers the
  PMP and programs its DART's address filter;
- the PMP's DART and mailbox.

The PMP report region stays disabled: no J604 consumer reads it (the
display vote goes through the PMP owner's RTKit session). The J713 also
enables it, and gives the MCC apple,boot-dma-devices; both are left for
the PMP and performance work.

This is the board-DTS form of the overlay in
commit 7852acbb7e12 ("arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Add an overlay that hands the PMP to Linux"),
so that the default J604 device tree carries what the display needs. /arm-io/pmp, /arm-io/dart-pmp and /arm-io/pmp/iop-pmp-nub of the
25G83 and 26B123 j604ap device trees match the J713's except for
phandles and the board's lts-config and lts-clpc-voltage calibration,
which m1n1 copies at boot.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 22 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 008c746010..e8a773994a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 		atcphy1 = &atcphy1;
 		bluetooth0 = &bluetooth0;
 		keyboard = &keyboard;
+		pmp = &pmp;
 		wifi0 = &wifi0;
 	};
 
@@ -36,11 +37,13 @@
 	 * DAPF and reserves its firmware segments and DAPF windows; an m1n1
 	 * that hands the J604 AOP over disables it when this does not ask
 	 * for it. For the MTP m1n1 only checks that it is powered and leaves
-	 * its filter as iBoot set it. The PMP is not requested: no J604 node
-	 * uses it yet.
+	 * its filter as iBoot set it. The PMP is handed over and powered as on
+	 * the J713: the internal display takes its DISP power vote through it.
 	 */
 	chosen {
-		linux-enablement-mac,dapf-handoff = "/arm-io/aop", "/arm-io/mtp";
+		linux-enablement-mac,dapf-handoff = "/arm-io/aop", "/arm-io/mtp",
+			"/arm-io/pmp";
+		linux-enablement-mac,dapf-power-on-handoff = "/arm-io/pmp";
 	};
 
 	led-controller {
@@ -599,6 +602,19 @@
  * for the J604, the AOP driver finds no memory-region and fails its probe
  * before touching the AOP, and the cards below never bind.
  */
+/*
+ * The PMP itself stays disabled here: m1n1 copies this Mac's board and
+ * DRAM values and the iop-pmp-nub tunables from the Apple device tree onto
+ * it and enables it (dt_set_pmp()). Its DART and mailbox are enabled here.
+ */
+&pmp_dart {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&pmp_mbox {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &aop {
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-AUD-1, DTV-AUD-2, DTV-AUD-13 */
 };
